---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ConversionActions from '../components/ConversionActions.astro';
import Portrait from '../components/Portrait.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Kiran Sabne, PostgreSQL Performance Engineer | WalStack" description="I’m Kiran Sabne, an independent PostgreSQL engineer in India. I investigate slow databases myself and work asynchronously with SaaS engineering teams.">
  <header class="container hero intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">India · remote, worldwide</p><h1>I'm Kiran Sabne.</h1>
    <p class="lede">When a release slows your product down, you want to know what changed and what you can safely undo. That's the question I started WalStack to answer.</p></div><Portrait /></header>
  <section><div class="container prose"><h2>My background</h2>
    <p>I've worked in database and backend engineering for about 8 years. About 6 of those years have focused on PostgreSQL in production, including RDS and Aurora.</p>
    <p>I've moved large tables, split them into smaller pieces called partitions, and upgraded databases between major versions. I've built pipelines that copy changes as they happen so other systems stay in sync.</p>
    <h2>What working with me looks like</h2>
    <p>I work alone, part-time, alongside a full-time job. I take a few engagements each month. I read the output, investigate the cause and write your report myself.</p>
    <p>I start with read-only information. You can run my scripts, inspect the output and remove sensitive details before sharing it.</p>
    <p>I'm based in India. Most work happens by email, with overlap for calls during US mornings and UK/EU afternoons.</p>
    <h2>Where to find my work</h2>
    <p>I built <a href={site.planReaderUrl} data-track="planreader_click">PlanReader</a> to help engineers read query plans. My experimental PostgreSQL extension, <a href={site.extensionUrl}>pg_stat_index_queries</a>, connects indexes to the queries that use them.</p>
    <p>WalStack is <a href={site.directoryUrl}>listed in PostgreSQL.org's Professional Services directory</a>. You can also find me on <a href={site.linkedinUrl}>LinkedIn</a> and <a href={site.githubUrl}>GitHub</a>.</p>
    <ConversionActions />
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
